- **Need to support multiple simultaneous simulator instances**  
  Then state tracking must evolve from a single `simPid` to instance-aware process/window discovery.

**Advanced alternative:** use `open -a` plus post-launch PID discovery.  
I would only do this if direct binary launch proves incompatible, because it is more brittle and offers no logging advantage.

--- 

If you want the smallest safe implementation order: **(1) direct-launch simulator binary, (2) make screenshot skip the stale PID check on macOS, (3) add `pdc` synthetic fallback diagnostics, (4) improve sim_log messaging.**

